A smooth straight stroke 5 km tall, against the same line made crooked ten ways (as the page has it):
   from 1000 m: the smooth one peaks at 0.01729, with 99.8% of its energy in the first fiftieth of a second; the crooked ones peak at 0.00846 to 0.01588 (the smooth one above 10 of 10) and have 3.0 times its energy on average
   from 2000 m: the smooth one peaks at 0.00982, with 99.8% of its energy in the first fiftieth of a second; the crooked ones peak at 0.00498 to 0.00890 (the smooth one above 10 of 10) and have 4.6 times its energy on average
   from 3000 m: the smooth one peaks at 0.00560, with 99.5% of its energy in the first fiftieth of a second; the crooked ones peak at 0.00323 to 0.00602 (the smooth one above 9 of 10) and have 8.5 times its energy on average
   from 4000 m: the smooth one peaks at 0.00290, with 98.7% of its energy in the first fiftieth of a second; the crooked ones peak at 0.00269 to 0.00530 (the smooth one above 3 of 10) and have 19.9 times its energy on average
   from 5000 m: the smooth one peaks at 0.00156, with 96.7% of its energy in the first fiftieth of a second; the crooked ones peak at 0.00236 to 0.00426 (the smooth one above 0 of 10) and have 45.3 times its energy on average
   from 6000 m: the smooth one peaks at 0.00090, with 95.1% of its energy in the first fiftieth of a second; the crooked ones peak at 0.00211 to 0.00318 (the smooth one above 0 of 10) and have 87.7 times its energy on average
   from 8000 m: the smooth one peaks at 0.00036, with 92.9% of its energy in the first fiftieth of a second; the crooked ones peak at 0.00161 to 0.00215 (the smooth one above 0 of 10) and have 273.7 times its energy on average
   from 9000 m: the smooth one peaks at 0.00024, with 88.8% of its energy in the first fiftieth of a second; the crooked ones peak at 0.00125 to 0.00238 (the smooth one above 0 of 10) and have 426.4 times its energy on average
